  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining System Architecture**\n\nI\'ve started sketching out the system architecture. My focus is now on the `server.ts` file, where I\'m setting up an Express server to listen on port 3000, bound to 0.0.0.0. Vite\'s middleware will handle development, and I\'m planning REST endpoints for health checks and some function called `gem`.\n\n\n**Developing API Endpoints**\n\nI\'m now focusing on API endpoint design. I\'ve outlined endpoints for AI-driven idea generation (`/api/gemini/`), technical guides (`/api/gemini/technical-guide`), and change request analysis (`/api/gemini/evaluate-change`). I\'m also planning CRUD operations for managing Brands, Territories, Assets, Bookings, Deliverables, and Audit Logs, along with associated validation rules, using an in-memory persistent database. Routes for schemas and documentation are on the roadmap, too. Finally, I\'m working on `/src/types/index.ts` to define types and interfaces such as user roles.\n\n\n**Modeling Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the database models. I\'m fleshing out details for Brands, Communication Territories, Digital Brand Assets, Hardware Equipment, Equipment Reservations, and Deliverables. Each model has core attributes like IDs, names, and creation timestamps, along with specific properties. For example, Equipment includes specs and rates, while Deliverables will be a key central object.\n\n\n**Refining Data Models**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refining data models. I\'ve defined aspects for the Technical Guide model, including aspect ratios, frame rates, color spaces, audio specs, and shot lists. The ChangeRequest model now includes fields for categorizing changes (script, visual, audio, schedule), a `isWithinTMinus3` flag, and director notes. I also have state transition definitions and ERD specs.\n\nI\'ve also built a fully loaded, realistic mock dataset in `initialData.ts`. It includes user accounts for a WebAdmin, a Director, and two collaborators, along with six initial brands/clients.\n\n\n**Populating Mock Data**\n\nI\'ve populated a detailed mock dataset. It now includes six brands: Apex Athletics, Lumina Skin, Kuro Artisan Coffee, Velox Electric, Terra Organics, and Nova FinTech, each with its own set of territories. I\'ve also populated the hardware inventory with over 15 realistic items. Finally, I\'ve created 12 sample deliverables with associated guides, equipment bookings, and change request records.\n\n**Designing UI Components**\n\nI\'m now designing the user interface components. I\'ve started with `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`, which includes a Current Role Switcher, Brand selector filter, Quick Search, Notifications, and System Status. I\'m also implementing `/src/components/RoleGate.tsx` and RBAC helper hooks for permission evaluation. The `/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx` component is next, for a multidimensional Kanban board.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `/src/components` directory. I\'m building out a `/src/components/DualCalendar.tsx` component with dynamic date ranges, toggles, and status indicators. I\'m also working on `BrandTerritoryManager.tsx` for brand and territory management. I\'m designing an Equipment Manager and a Technical Guide Viewer with AI integration.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 351193010
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
