  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on the user interface components. I\'ve started listing the necessary ones, specifically `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`. This includes the role switcher dropdown, incorporating instant persona preview and an active permissions summary, alongside a brand selector filter.\n\n\n**Expanding Kanban Components**\n\nNow I\'m diving deeper into the Kanban board. I\'ve broken it down into columns and detailed each card\'s elements like brand badges, territory tags, collaborators, priority, and actions. I\'m also including filter options and a modal for new deliverables. The `/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx` structure is taking shape, and should offer a clear and rich user experience.\n\n\n**Developing Date & Resource Tools**\n\nI\'m now deep into the calendar and resource management components. I\'m building a dual calendar component, `/src/components/DualCalendar.tsx`, that offers date switching and detailed views with badges for key data. Concurrently, the brand/territory manager is taking shape, and then the equipment manager, with its real-time collision detection for resource reservations, will be created. The pieces are all coming together.\n\n\n**Constructing Technical Guides**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `/src/components/TechnicalGuideViewer.tsx` component. This guide will be structured around each deliverable, and will include aspects such as aspect ratios, framerates, color profiles, audio specs, shotlists, equipment assignments, and the director\'s sign-off. I\'m also including a \"Compile with Gemini AI\" button, which will auto-generate shotlists and specifications. Finally, I\'m working on the deliverable detail modal with a timeline and change request system.\n\n\n**Refining AI & System Components**\n\nI\'m expanding the AI Copilot modal, now `/src/components/AICopilotModal.tsx`, into a multi-mode assistant. This includes an Idea Generator grounded in trends and brand territories, a Technical Guide Compiler offering shotlists and color profiles with a thinking mode, and a T-3 Change Impact Evaluator that analyzes risks and delays. Concurrently, `/src/components/SystemSpecsHub.tsx` is taking shape, featuring an interactive ERD, a state machine, API contracts with OpenAPI specs, and a mock JSON dataset for initial testing. The Director will have override approval capabilities as well.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 9
      nanos: 87054638
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
