    session_summary: "This summary outlines the current state of the **CineFlow Studio OS** project and the pending task to apply the \"High Density\" design theme.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Apply \"High Density\" Design Theme:** The user has provided an HTML/CSS snippet for a \"High Density\" theme and requested that the current application adopt this aesthetic.\n    *   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION (Pending).\n    *   **Instructions:** \"Extract ONLY the styling (colors, fonts, spacing, borders, shadows, backgrounds, gradients) and layout patterns... Do NOT replace or restructure the existing app\'s HTML elements \342\200\224 preserve all existing components, content, and functionality. Only modify CSS/styling and adjust layout containers as needed.\"\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Design Constraints:** The user explicitly mandated preserving the existing HTML structure and functionality while updating the visual layer.\n*   **Theme Source:** The user provided a complete HTML/CSS snippet representing the \"High Density\" theme, which includes a specific color palette (e.g., `#f1f3f5` background, `#1a1c1e` sidebar) and layout density (e.g., `text-xs`, `grid-cols-12`).\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **System Architecture:** Successfully implemented the core CineFlow Studio OS, including:\n    *   **RBAC & Governance:** Built `WebAdminDashboard` with role-based access control and audit logging.\n    *   **Technical Documentation:** Created `SystemSpecsHub` containing ERD (Mermaid/DBML), State Machine logic, API contracts, and dataset export functionality.\n    *   **Core Application:** Set up `App.tsx` with routing for Kanban, Calendar, Brands, Equipment, Specs, and Admin modules.\n    *   **Data Layer:** Implemented `initialData.ts` with a full snapshot of the system state (`INITIAL_DATA_SNAPSHOT`).\n    *   **Styling Infrastructure:** Configured custom scrollbars in `index.css` to handle dense UI elements.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture & Interfaces:**\n    *   The app uses `AppContext` (in `src/context/AppContext.tsx`) as the single source of truth for global state (users, brands, deliverables, etc.).\n    *   `Navbar.tsx` handles navigation and persona switching (RBAC simulator).\n    *   `KanbanBoard.tsx` is the primary view, utilizing a 7-phase lifecycle column structure.\n*   **Constraints:** The application relies on `lucide-react` for iconography and Tailwind CSS for styling. The current theme is dark-mode centric (`bg-zinc-950`), while the requested \"High Density\" theme is light-mode centric (`bg-[#f1f3f5]`).\n*   **Dependencies:** The project uses React 19 and Tailwind CSS.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/SystemSpecsHub.tsx`: Created to house technical documentation.\n    *   `/src/components/WebAdminDashboard.tsx`: Created for administrative control and monitoring.\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`: Created as the main entry point and layout shell.\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Edited to add custom scrollbar styles.\n    *   `/src/data/initialData.ts`: Edited to export `INITIAL_DATA_SNAPSHOT`.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Investigated for navigation and role-switching logic.\n    *   `/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx`: Investigated for layout structure and deliverable management.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Immediate Task:** Implement the \"High Density\" design theme.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    1.  **Theme Analysis:** Map the provided \"High Density\" CSS (backgrounds, text colors, spacing) to Tailwind utility classes.\n    2.  **Global Update:** Update `index.css` or global styles to accommodate the new light-mode color scheme.\n    3.  **Component Refactoring:** Iteratively update the main layout (`App.tsx`) and key components (`Navbar.tsx`, `KanbanBoard.tsx`) to match the density and styling of the provided design, ensuring that the existing component logic (e.g., role switching, kanban movement) remains fully functional.\n    4.  **Verification:** Ensure that the \"High Density\" layout does not break the responsiveness or the specific business rules (like the T-3 window alert)."
