  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Canvas**\n\nI\'ve initiated the aesthetic definition, focusing initially on the background. I\'m leaning toward a neutral, light gray such as `#f1f3f5` or `bg-[#f1f3f5]` for the page body and canvas. I\'m also now considering the core text color and am comparing `#343a40`, `text-slate-800`, and `text-slate-900`. Next, I\'ll explore options for the design of the cards and containers, which are meant to have a clean, light aesthetic.\n\n\n**Refining Container Styles**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the card and container designs, settling on `bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-xs rounded-lg` for general use. For high-density headers, I\'ve defined `bg-slate-50 border-b border-slate-200 px-3.5 py-2` with specific text styling. Inset fields use `bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-md p-2`. I\'ve also established a dark accent for special elements with `bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 text-slate-100 rounded-lg`. Finally, I am currently working on navigation with `bg-white border-b border-slate-200 shadow`.\n\n\n**Defining Navigation Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing navigation elements. The tab bar will use `bg-white border-t border-slate-200`. Active tabs may be `bg-blue-50 text-blue-700` or `bg-slate-900 text-white`. Inactive tabs use hover effects. I have also designed search input styles, as well as brand and filter dropdowns. The kanban board design is next. I am also planning the dual calendar.\n\n\n**Designing the Calendar**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the calendar component. The container itself will be `bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-lg shadow-xs overflow-hidden`. Weekday headers will be `bg-slate-50 border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-600 font-bold text-xs py-2`. Day cells will use `bg-white divide-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-50/80 min-h-[115px] p-2 border-r border-b border-slate-200`, with highlights for today using `bg-blue-50/40 ring-1 ring-inset ring-blue-400`. I have also specified event pill styles.\n\nI have also started styling the Brand & Territory Manager elements, as well as the Equipment Manager elements.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
