    session_summary: "# 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Apply \"High Density\" Design Theme:** The user has requested a visual overhaul of the entire application to a \"High Density\" theme (light-mode centric, dense layout, specific typography).\n    *   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION.\n    *   **Instructions:** Preserve existing HTML structure and functionality; modify only CSS/styling and layout containers.\n    *   **Remaining Scope:** Migrate individual components: `BrandTerritoryManager`, `WebAdminDashboard`, `SystemSpecsHub`, `DeliverableDetailModal`, and `AICopilotModal`.\n\n# 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Design Constraints:** The user explicitly mandated preserving the existing HTML structure and functionality while updating the visual layer.\n*   **Theme Source:** The user provided a complete HTML/CSS snippet representing the \"High Density\" theme, which includes a specific color palette (e.g., `#f1f3f5` background) and layout density (e.g., `text-xs`).\n*   **Scope:** The project is a \"Studio OS\" for managing creative workflows, including RBAC, Kanban boards, and equipment reservations.\n*   **Business Logic:** The user emphasized that business logic (e.g., T-3 window alerts, equipment collision detection, territory validation rules) must remain intact during the visual migration.\n\n# 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **System Architecture:** Successfully implemented core CineFlow Studio OS, including RBAC, `WebAdminDashboard` (initial), `SystemSpecsHub` (initial), `App.tsx` routing, and custom scrollbar infrastructure.\n*   **Visual Migration (High Density):**\n    *   **Global Styles:** Updated `/src/index.css` to define the new light-mode color palette, system typography, and scrollbar styles.\n    *   **Layout Shell:** Updated `/src/App.tsx` to use the new light background (`#f1f3f5`) and adjusted main viewport padding and footer styling.\n    *   **Navbar:** Updated `/src/components/Navbar.tsx` to match the High Density aesthetic.\n    *   **KanbanBoard:** Migrated to the new color palette, layout density, and updated the \"New Deliverable\" modal.\n    *   **DualCalendar:** Migrated to the new color palette, layout density, and updated the view toggle and legend styles.\n\n# 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture & Interfaces:**\n    *   `AppContext` (in `src/context/AppContext.tsx`) is the single source of truth for global state.\n    *   The UI relies on `lucide-react` for iconography and Tailwind CSS for styling.\n*   **Theme Shift:** The application is transitioning from a dark-mode centric (`bg-zinc-950`) to a light-mode centric (`bg-[#f1f3f5]`) design.\n*   **UI Patterns:** The application makes extensive use of modal-based interactions (`DeliverableDetailModal`, `AICopilotModal`, `EquipmentManager`).\n*   **Constraint:** Business logic (e.g., T-3 window alerts, equipment collision detection) must remain functional after CSS changes.\n\n# 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Updated global body styles, scrollbars, and typography.\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`: Updated main layout shell, background, and footer.\n    *   `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Updated component styling.\n    *   `/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx`: Updated to High Density light-mode aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/DualCalendar.tsx`: Updated to High Density light-mode aesthetic.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/BrandTerritoryManager.tsx`:\n        *   **File Landscape:** Manages brand-specific communication territories and digital assets. Contains complex forms for CRUD operations on territories and assets.\n        *   **Key Focused Sections:** The entire file needs migration to the High Density theme, specifically the grid layouts for territories/assets and the modal forms.\n\n# 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Current Work:** We have successfully migrated the global shell, `Navbar`, `KanbanBoard`, and `DualCalendar`.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    1.  **Migrate `BrandTerritoryManager.tsx`:** This is the next logical component to migrate to the High Density theme. It involves updating the brand selector, territory cards, and asset cards to the new light-mode aesthetic.\n    2.  **Migrate `WebAdminDashboard.tsx`:** Update the health stats cards and RBAC table.\n    3.  **Migrate remaining modals/components:** Iteratively apply the theme to `DeliverableDetailModal`, `AICopilotModal`, and `SystemSpecsHub.tsx`."
