    session_summary: "This summary updates the project status following the recent migration of key modal components to the \"High Density\" design theme.\n\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n*   **Apply \"High Density\" Design Theme:** The user has requested a comprehensive visual overhaul of the application to a \"High Density\" theme (light-mode centric, dense layout, specific typography).\n    *   **Status:** IMPLEMENTATION.\n    *   **Instructions:** Preserve existing HTML structure and functionality; modify only CSS/styling and layout containers.\n    *   **Remaining Scope:** Migrate `AICopilotModal.tsx`.\n*   **Preserve Business Logic:** All functional logic (e.g., T-3 window alerts, equipment collision detection, territory validation rules) must remain intact during the visual migration.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n*   **Design Constraints:** The user explicitly mandated preserving the existing HTML structure and functionality while updating the visual layer.\n*   **Theme Source:** The user provided a complete HTML/CSS snippet representing the \"High Density\" theme, which includes a specific color palette (e.g., `#f1f3f5` background) and layout density (e.g., `text-xs`).\n*   **Scope:** The project is a \"Studio OS\" for managing creative workflows, including RBAC, Kanban boards, and equipment reservations.\n*   **Business Logic:** The user emphasized that business logic (e.g., T-3 window alerts, equipment collision detection, territory validation rules) must remain functional after CSS changes.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n*   **System Architecture:** Successfully implemented core CineFlow Studio OS, including RBAC, `WebAdminDashboard`, `SystemSpecsHub`, `App.tsx` routing, and custom scrollbar infrastructure.\n*   **Visual Migration (High Density):**\n    *   **Global Styles:** Updated `/src/index.css` (global body styles, scrollbars, typography).\n    *   **Layout Shell:** Updated `/src/App.tsx` (main layout shell, background, footer).\n    *   **Components:** Successfully migrated the following to the High Density light-mode aesthetic:\n        *   `Navbar.tsx`\n        *   `KanbanBoard.tsx`\n        *   `DualCalendar.tsx`\n        *   `BrandTerritoryManager.tsx`\n        *   `EquipmentManager.tsx`\n        *   `WebAdminDashboard.tsx`\n        *   `SystemSpecsHub.tsx`\n        *   `DeliverableDetailModal.tsx` (includes T-3 logic and tabbed navigation).\n        *   `TechnicalGuideViewer.tsx` (includes shotlist management and director sign-off logic).\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n*   **Architecture & Interfaces:**\n    *   `AppContext` (in `src/context/AppContext.tsx`) is the single source of truth for global state.\n    *   The UI relies on `lucide-react` for iconography and Tailwind CSS for styling.\n*   **Theme Shift:** The application has transitioned from a dark-mode centric (`bg-zinc-950`) to a light-mode centric (`bg-white` / `bg-slate-50`) design.\n*   **UI Patterns:** The application makes extensive use of modal-based interactions.\n*   **Constraint:** Business logic (e.g., T-3 window alerts, equipment collision detection) must remain functional after CSS changes.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Updated global body styles, scrollbars, and typography.\n    *   `/src/App.tsx`: Updated main layout shell, background, and footer.\n    *   `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Updated component styling.\n    *   `/src/components/KanbanBoard.tsx`: Updated to High Density light-mode aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/DualCalendar.tsx`: Updated to High Density light-mode aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/BrandTerritoryManager.tsx`: Migrated to High Density aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/EquipmentManager.tsx`: Migrated to High Density aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/WebAdminDashboard.tsx`: Migrated to High Density aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/SystemSpecsHub.tsx`: Migrated to High Density aesthetic.\n    *   `/src/components/DeliverableDetailModal.tsx`: Migrated to High Density light-mode aesthetic; preserved T-3 logic and tabbed navigation.\n    *   `/src/components/TechnicalGuideViewer.tsx`: Migrated to High Density light-mode aesthetic; preserved shotlist management and director sign-off logic.\n*   **Viewed Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/AICopilotModal.tsx`:\n        *   **File Landscape:** Contains AI chat/ideation interface, technical guide compiler, and logic for creating deliverables.\n        *   **Status:** Pending High Density migration.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n*   **Current Work:** We have successfully migrated the global shell and all major components, including the complex `DeliverableDetailModal` and `TechnicalGuideViewer`.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    1.  **Migrate `AICopilotModal.tsx`:** Apply the High Density theme to the AI chat interface, ensuring the ideation and technical guide compilation forms remain functional."
